  "notes": "tomHighAcousticSeed: the deep head WITHOUT wires — picked by ear as \"the only\nhigh tom that sounds good\" (2026-09-30). History: the first high tom was the\nfitted acoustic layering at 225 Hz (heard as \"so organic, but a high tom —\nhigh pitched and hollow, almost conga like\"), shipped WITH the wire layer,\nthen heard to \"rattle throughout\" (fingerprint.TailRattle 663); removing the\nwires fixed the rattle, but in the round-3 A/B only this deeper head passed as\na tom. A tom has no snare wires.",
